Good morning,

We are instructed to notify damage to a third party's rooftop plant on behalf of our client Tidewater Roofing & Exteriors, LLC. Our reference is CB/ROOF/2024/3376. The client's operations manager is away with the certificate file, so please locate on our reference - it is the commercial liability policy we placed for them that renewed last November.

Broker reference: CB/ROOF/2024/3376
Insured name: Tidewater Roofing & Exteriors, LLC
Insured licence: Virginia Class A Contractor 2705-118442
Date of loss: 26 August 2025
Loss location: 1900 Bainbridge Logistics Way, Chesapeake, VA 23320
Cause: Crane load swung into a tenant's rooftop condensing units
Estimated loss: USD 182,000

A bundle of insulation and membrane being flown to Roof Section 7 caught the guy
wires and then the housings on a tenant's rooftop condensing bank and dragged
across it. Nothing was dropped and nobody was hurt.

The equipment belongs to the tenant in Suite 400, not to the building owner and
not to our client. It is their process refrigeration for a 22,000 sq ft
temperature-controlled fulfilment area and it is down. They have spot coolers and
a rental chiller in and are saying they have product at risk. The property manager
has put our client on notice for the equipment, the refrigerant, the temporary
cooling and any product and business interruption.

Nothing on the tenant's equipment has been touched, straightened or repaired.
Our client paid USD 3,800 for the first two days of spot coolers directly, which
we flag as a possible voluntary payment point.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * lifting incident report
  * tenant damage schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. Our client would also like your
view on the crane company's position - their hire contract has our client
indemnifying them, which we are not happy about.

